# Most of what this file used to hold is gone, and not because the rules were
# wrong. Generated artifacts — conda envs, container tarballs, ENV/RUN reports,
# sealed specs, drafts, job state, transfer receipts, reference data — no longer
# live in the checkout at all. They resolve through agent/skills/workspace.py into
# a workspace outside it, and tests/test_workspace_resolution.py fails the build if
# one comes back. "Artifacts never reach GitHub" is structural now rather than
# maintained by a list somebody has to remember to extend.

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo
.Python
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.env
.venv
venv/
.pytest_cache/

# The agent's own runtime env — created per-clone by scripts/setup.sh; the
# launcher (start_mcp_server.sh) and bootstrap wrapper resolve it by this path.
.conda_runtime/

# Private miniforge — installed by scripts/setup.sh only on machines with no
# conda anywhere (with consent). Repo-local, no shell integration.
.miniforge/

# The workspace pointer — one line naming where this clone keeps its generated
# artifacts. Written by scripts/setup.sh; per-machine, like the runtime env.
/.bioinf_workspace

# The agent's command-and-control file lives at the WORKSPACE root, so nothing
# should be writing it here. Kept as a belt-and-braces rule anyway: it carries
# real cluster hostnames, usernames and paths, and the cost of the rule is one
# line against the cost of the mistake. The glob covers the .bak sidecar, because
# a backup of a secret is a secret. The tracked template (generic placeholders
# only) is agent/skills/projects_access.yaml.example.
/projects_access.yaml*

# Outcome-model coverage artifacts (transient; measured, not authored). These DO
# belong in the checkout — they are inputs to docs/outcomes_ledger.json, which is
# tracked.
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.json

# The outcomes dashboard is a VIEW — a pure render of two tracked records
# (outcomes_ledger.json + terminal_coverage.json), with zero byte-readers in
# tests or CI. Tracking it made every pair of parallel branches conflict on a
# file whose only correct merge is a re-render. scripts/refresh_meters.sh
# rebuilds it; the records stay tracked and ratcheted.
docs/outcomes_dashboard.html

# Advisory flock sentinels (agent/skills/store_lock.py), runtime only.
*.lock

# Claude Code session lock — runtime sentinel, regenerated per session.
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
